#  webkit-wpe-preconnect-api.patch: let the embedder warm a connection before
#  the user commits to a navigation.
#  WebKit already implements speculative connections end to end — WebPageProxy
#  ::preconnectTo() -> NetworkProcess::preconnectTo() -> PreconnectTask, with
#  ENABLE(SERVER_PRECONNECT) on for every glib port and allowsServerPreconnect
#  defaulting true — but no WPE public API reaches it, so on this browser the
#  whole DNS/TCP/TLS handshake runs serially AFTER the tap commits. Exports
#  wpe_sfos_preconnect() so the UI can start it at intent time (touch-down on a
#  link, URL-bar completion) instead. Nothing is fetched: only a socket is
#  opened and the TLS handshake is performed.
#
# ---
Speculative connection API for the WPE GLib API.

The cost this targets is not rendering. On a phone radio, a cold origin costs a
DNS round trip, a TCP handshake and a TLS handshake before the first request
byte can leave — commonly 200-500 ms, and all of it currently sits after the
user's finger lifts, because the navigation is the first thing that touches the
network.

Every piece of the machinery is already present and enabled in our build:

  * `ENABLE_SERVER_PRECONNECT` is 1 for all glib ports
    (Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnableGlib.h:58).
  * `WebsiteDataStoreConfiguration::m_allowsServerPreconnect` defaults true
    (WebsiteDataStoreConfiguration.h:343), which is the gate
    `WebPageProxy::preconnectTo()` checks first.
  * `WebPageProxy::preconnectTo()` is public (WebPageProxy.h:1905) and does the
    right thing for a main-resource preconnect: it fills in the predicted user
    agent, sets first-party-for-cookies to the target, raises the priority and
    hands a `PreconnectTask` to the network process.

What is missing is only the public entry point. Cocoa reaches this from
WKWebView, GTK never exposed it either, so nothing in-tree could be copied —
hence a `wpe_sfos_*` export in the same style as wpe_sfos_set_dark_mode() and
wpe_sfos_set_page_scale().

Two properties worth stating because they decide how safely the embedder can
guess:

  * A preconnect sends no request. `PreconnectTask` sets
    `shouldPreconnectOnly = PreconnectOnly::Yes`, so soup opens the socket and
    completes TLS and stops. The path, query and fragment of @uri never leave
    the device; only scheme, host and port do (DNS, TCP, and the TLS SNI).
    Guessing wrong therefore costs an idle socket, not a page view.
  * The connection belongs to the view's own network session, so a preconnect
    issued from a private tab uses the ephemeral session, exactly like the load
    it is anticipating would.

Browser side: WPEWebPage::preconnect() rate-limits per origin and is driven by
the kPreconnectBridge user script (touch-down on a link) and the URL bar's
completion, both behind ATLANTIC_PRECONNECT (default off pending the A/B).

Ordering: appends to WebKitWebView.cpp after webkit-wpe-page-scale-api.patch.
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitWebView.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitWebView.cpp
@@ -6046,3 +6046,40 @@
 
     return getPage(webView).pageScaleFactor();
 }
+
+// SFOS: open a connection to @uri's origin without loading anything, so that a
+// navigation the embedder expects (finger down on a link, top URL-bar
+// completion) finds DNS resolved, the socket connected and TLS negotiated
+// instead of paying for all three after the tap commits.
+//
+// This is WebKit's own speculative-connection path — the one Cocoa drives from
+// WKWebView — which has no WPE API. It is a no-op unless the network session
+// allows server preconnect (default) and @uri is an http(s) URL.
+//
+// Nothing is fetched: PreconnectTask runs with PreconnectOnly::Yes, so no
+// request line is ever written and the path/query/fragment of @uri stay on the
+// device. The session used is the view's own, so private tabs preconnect on
+// their ephemeral session.
+//
+// Safe to call repeatedly: the network layer coalesces onto an existing
+// connection to the same origin. The embedder still rate-limits (see
+// WPEWebPage::preconnect) so a scroll over a link list cannot spray sockets.
+extern "C" __attribute__((visibility("default")))
+void wpe_sfos_preconnect(WebKitWebView* webView, const char* uri)
+{
+    g_return_if_fail(WEBKIT_IS_WEB_VIEW(webView));
+    g_return_if_fail(uri);
+
+    URL url { String::fromUTF8(uri) };
+    if (!url.isValid() || url.isEmpty() || !url.protocolIsInHTTPFamily())
+        return;
+
+    // Strip everything the connection cannot use anyway. A preconnect is keyed
+    // by origin, and NetworkLoadScheduler remembers the URL it was started for
+    // (startedPreconnectForMainResource) — keeping a guessed path out of that
+    // bookkeeping keeps the speculation from influencing a later real load.
+    url.removeQueryAndFragmentIdentifier();
+    url.setPath("/"_s);
+
+    getPage(webView).preconnectTo(ResourceRequest { WTF::move(url) });
+}
